{title: 098 - Can You Count the Stars?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #098 • GERMAN FOLK TUNE • 8.7.8.7.8.8.7.8}
{lyricist: Wilhelm Hey}
{composer: German Folk Tune}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 98}
{meta: tune GERMAN FOLK TUNE}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7.8.8.7.8}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Can you count [Eb]the stars that [Bb7/D]brightly
[Eb]Twinkle in the midnight [Bb7/D]sky?
[Bb7/D]Can you count the clouds, so [Eb]lightly
[Eb/Bb]O'er the meadows floating [Bb7/D]by?
[Eb]God, the Lord, doth [Bb7/D]mark their number
[Eb]With His eyes [Bb]that never [Bb7]slumber;
[Eb]He hath made every [Bb]one,
[Bb]He hath [Bb7]made them [Eb]every one.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Can you count [Eb]the wings now [Bb7/D]flashing
[Eb]In the sunshine's golden [Bb7/D]light?
[Bb7/D]Can you count the fishes [Eb]splashing
[Eb/Bb]In the cooling waters [Bb7/D]bright?
[Eb]God, the Lord, a [Bb7/D]name hath given,
[Eb]To all creatures [Bb]under [Bb7]heaven;
[Eb]He hath named them every [Bb]one,
[Bb]He hath [Bb7]named them [Eb]every one.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Do you know [Eb]how many [Bb7/D]children
[Eb]Rise each morning blithe [Bb7/D]and gay?
[Bb7/D]Can you count their jolly [Eb]voices,
[Eb/Bb]Singing sweetly day [Bb7/D]by day?
[Eb]God hears all the [Bb7/D]happy voices,
[Eb]In their merry [Bb]songs rejoices;
[Eb]And He loves them, every [Bb]one,
[Bb]And He [Bb7]loves them, [Eb]every one.
{end_of_verse}
